ited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-12T03:09:10-07:00","id":1234225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1233597-monday-meeting-origins-pdf-coming-out-to-backers-this-week?p=1234195#post1234195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obviously arranging Associated Purviews for the Gods is far more art than science, and no one is every going to make a list that fits everyone's interpretation, and its the simplest possible matter to adjust at one's own table - but how does Artemis not have Wild?</div> </div> </div> </div>At the very least, her Roman Mantle Diana will have it at my table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-12T06:27:57-07:00","id":1234265,"title":"","content":"Echoing the sentiment. That opening fiction was absolutely tops. I cackled like a maniacal child.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18560-saedar","name":"saedar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-12T08:44:32-07:00","id":1234295,"title":"","content":"Well Scion: Origins did it. I backed the Kickstarter only at the Origin level as I was hesitant to go all in. After looking through it today, I'll be adding Scion: Hero to my Backerkit. I'm already thinking about alternate time periods to run Scion in.<br /> <br /> Well done Onyx Path, you have earned more of my money.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Lead Writer for the Savage Age of Werewolf: the Apocalypse: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/428750/Ghost-Lineages-The-Advanced-Players-Guide-to-the-Savage-Age\" target=\"_blank\">Ghost Lineages</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/312700/The-Rise-of-the-Garou-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Two\" target=\"_blank\">Rise of the Garou</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/331302/Tools-of-Extinction-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Three\" target=\"_blank\">Tools of Extinction</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/352717/Tribebook-Wlewa\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook: Wlewa</a>.<br /> <br /> Want RPGs in libraries? Check out my book, <a href=\"http://www.abc-clio.com/ABC-CLIOCorporate/product.aspx?pc=A3951P\" target=\"_blank\">Dragons in the Stacks</a>. Now with <a href=\"http://www.ennie-awards.com/blog/2015-ennie-award-nominees-and-spotlight-winners/\" target=\"_blank\">awards</a>!<br /> \u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1813-grimjaws","name":"grimjaws","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1813_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-12T16:33:36-07:00","id":1234438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saedar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1233597-monday-meeting-origins-pdf-coming-out-to-backers-this-week?p=1234265#post1234265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Echoing the sentiment. That opening fiction was absolutely tops. I cackled like a maniacal child.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;I could pick one of them and earn two enemies... Or I could be bold and become legendary.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T00:40:35-07:00","id":1234556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1233597-monday-meeting-origins-pdf-coming-out-to-backers-this-week?p=1234438#post1234438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;I could pick one of them and earn two enemies... Or I could be bold and become legendary.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder though, if he had of picked one of them, would he have been from then on the adopted child of Hera or Athena? Of course if he chose his mother he would have simply been one of her Scion's but still.<br /> <br /> Also, while I found this story to be outstanding. I couldn't help but think of Aphrodite as some sort of Kawaii depiction. For the Goddess of Love... this seems....lacking. I feel as though she should have been more commanding, more at home within her own sensuality and sexuality. When it comes to beauty, she should be leaving Hera and Athena in the dust. She IS desire, lust and seduction. Not some sort of helpless damsel in need of a rescue.<br /> <br /> Less this...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/vTzo2h3\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/vTzo2h3\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/vTzo2h3\" target=\"_blank\"> https://imgur.com/a/vTzo2h3 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> and more this...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--previe